+## Failure cleanup
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, `onError` receives the session and that same error, `afterSession` then receives the session, and the original error still rejects the caller ([validated by: reports and cleans up a beforeSession failure before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSessionFailure.acceptance.test.ts#L12)).
+- Because `beforeSession` can fail after doing only part of its setup, `afterSession` must treat the session as potentially partially initialized and clean up only resources that were actually allocated.
